**Guzzle version(s) affected**: 6.3.3

**Description**  

Request to cyrillic domain fails.

**How to reproduce**  

```
$httpClient = new \GuzzleHttp\Client();
$response = $httpClient->get('https://русские-домены.рф');
echo (string)$response->getBody();
```
**Possible Solution**  

It fails due to *Host* header in `GuzzleHttp\Psr7\Request::updateHostFromUri()`
Header must be converted using `idn_to_ascii()` function.

**Additional context**  

But it works using `curl`

```
$ch = curl_init('https://русские-домены.рф');
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
$html = curl_exec($ch);
curl_close($ch);
echo $html;
```

Handling of query parameters with the same name has changed in v3.8:

``` PHP
<?php

require 'vendor/autoload.php';
use Guzzle\Http\Client;

$client = new Client('http://en.wikipedia.org');
$request = $client->get(array('wiki/Guzzle{?foo*}', array('foo' => array('bar', 'baz'))));
$response = $request->send();

echo $response->getEffectiveUrl();

// 3.7.4
// http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guzzle?foo=bar&foo=baz
// 3.8.0
// http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guzzle?foo%5B0%5D=bar&foo%5B1%5D=baz 

```

According to http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6570#section-3.2.1, the behavior in 3.7.4 is the correct one.

